  "body": "**What happens.** The release run for v0.20.0 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/43644441134) fails in the `linux` job, at step \"Assemble Linux packages\". `rpmbuild` stops with this error:\n\n```\nerror: Installed (but unpackaged) file(s) found:\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/{16,32,48,64,128,256,512}x…/apps/camcraft.png\n```\n\nThus the release has no Linux packages (rpm, deb, AppImage, tar.gz).\n\n**Cause.** Commit 55c8bcc6 (`feat(packaging): the logotype in the exe, installer, .icns and Linux icons`) installs the hicolor icons in `scripts/package-linux.sh` (lines 67-71). The `%files` list of the RPM spec in the same script (line 117) does not name them.\n\n**Fix.** Add this line to the `%files` list:\n\n```\n/usr/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps/camcraft.png\n```\n\n**Done means:** `scripts/package-linux.sh` builds the rpm, and a release run of the fix makes all Linux packages. The maintainer decides how v0.20.0 gets its Linux packages: a re-run from a fixed ref, or the next release.\n",
